-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2299650c40ea59097f3707e7d99960e2fdc422f1c2f77026d41fa2eb4f83839b","event_uuid":"d2deeb4d-4ee0-4682-87ce-4ec6b71ccbf2","position":{"commit_sha":"fb1b195e241c33dcc30af09f64972fbd0859b789","position":"1786053166099213001-d2deeb4d-4ee0-4682-87ce-4ec6b71ccbf2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a5be154dc318ff57f93645f4173f0de4a3772ebb4427d10c56c2ec66a445b4f8","event_uuid":"ed32c287-8995-4fd7-bc05-4d721b70e5ea","position":{"commit_sha":"fb1b195e241c33dcc30af09f64972fbd0859b789","position":"1786053166675887001-ed32c287-8995-4fd7-bc05-4d721b70e5ea"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"4f7c900f9202db77c6a3ace05c7b8a81084b5b2e94f61c8d450d3e0db53baa75","event_uuid":"da9d42cc-baf3-4eba-8e75-93fb6f193bdc","position":{"commit_sha":"eb5b6bc888a348c24b91fbe7dfaf7a24ea12989c","position":"1786056122934869001-da9d42cc-baf3-4eba-8e75-93fb6f193bdc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bc9bb49d5bacf77974d4b1a189a01e53a48e8d52875f2b49279835a2b3c3e980","event_uuid":"a3681f44-9877-452e-9db8-339f5f671ecd","position":{"commit_sha":"f3506ba17335b88850a99263a81f09386f778968","position":"1786056142897165001-a3681f44-9877-452e-9db8-339f5f671ecd"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"SECOND live capture, hours after the first: closing epic 9b71-55b3-1bd1-4a97. Primary verifier run exhausted on GENUINE BREADTH (requests=240, distinct_ratio_window=1.0, max_consecutive_repeat=1 — the c827 guard correctly did not fire; an epic spanning 7 children exceeds the flat budget). Recovery started and ONE evidence run hit its 20-request budget with a healthy profile (distinct_ratio_window=0.958) — and the whole recovery died again: 'bounded evidence recovery also failed', exit offered --force-close. This bug is now the single remaining blocker for closing the loop-breaker epic itself. Also folded the plan-review G6 finding into the plan: the catch set now includes token-exhaustion UnretryableOutputError (guarded by _is_token_exhaustion, mirroring run()), since an evidence run emitting past its output cap would otherwise reinstate the defect through a third exception class.","timestamp":1785989291053192001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Live Bedrock proof (session experiment, AWS us-east-1, model bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6):\n\nDrove CompletionAgentStep._recover over 3 criteria with a synthetic primary budget-exhaustion precondition. The FIRST criterion's evidence run was forced to raise LLMBudgetExhaustedError; the remaining 2 evidence runs and the tool-free finalizer went LIVE to Bedrock.\n\nResult:\n- evidence runs total = 3 (1 forced-exhausted -> content-free placeholder entry; 2 live Bedrock evidence runs)\n- finalizer live Bedrock calls = 1\n- recovery COMPLETED WITH A VERDICT: StepResult status=succeeded, completion_verdict returned with 3 criteria entries (verdict=FAIL, correctly, because one criterion carries the could-not-gather-within-bounds placeholder and cannot be affirmed).\n\nConclusion: a real gate-style recovery where one evidence run exhausts its budget now completes with a verdict instead of failing whole — the exhaustion-is-not-a-verdict trap is closed, and partial evidence is preserved. (Corroborated in production by the 8eb3 close, whose primary agentic verification hit a real runaway loop and recovered to a PASS verdict via this same path.)","timestamp":1786056122934869001}],"created_at":1785983869660728001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b30079f7-9321-4a5e-8292-bdfa3f62065d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"c827-2a23-cd00-473e"},{"link_uuid":"da3896c1-9570-47ec-ba76-d0b08ef89aaf","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2948-48e5-666f-4677"},{"link_uuid":"8db63530-75eb-427a-a9d3-db86b0cdb148","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f80f-7776-02aa-4091"}],"description":"Live capture (2026-08-06, closing c827-2a23-cd00-473e from the loop-breaker checkout, main at 9a27202837): the primary completion-verifier run looped and was correctly aborted by the c827 actuator (requests=119, distinct_ratio_window=0.5). Bounded recovery started, but the evidence agent for ONE criterion hit its own step budget with a perfectly HEALTHY profile — 'completion-verifier-evidence ... hit step budget (request_limit=20 max_iterations=40) requests=20 tool_calls=35 distinct=35 max_consecutive_repeat=1 distinct_ratio_window=1.0 top_repeats=[]' — and that single LLMBudgetExhaustedError propagated out of the per-criterion loop in CompletionAgentStep._recover (completion_recovery.py ~:519-536), discarding all evidence already gathered and failing the whole recovery. The gate then reported 'bounded evidence recovery also failed' and offered --force-close: the exact exhaustion-is-not-a-verdict trap this cluster removes, one layer down.\n\nThe defect: the per-criterion evidence loop treats a single criterion's budget exhaustion as fatal to the aggregate, when the bound is a per-criterion safeguard. Partial evidence must be preserved rather than discarded — the finalizer already renders per-criterion verdicts and can mark a criterion unverifiable-within-bounds.\n\nPlan: catch LLMBudgetExhaustedError, RunawayToolLoopError, and token-exhaustion UnretryableOutputError (guarded by _is_token_exhaustion, mirroring run()) around the per-criterion runner.run in _recover; substitute a content-free placeholder evidence entry that names the failure class and its usage counters (from the exception diagnostic), mark the entry exhausted=true; continue with remaining criteria; recovery fails outright only if EVERY criterion's evidence run fails. Placeholder text must never be presentable as affirmative evidence — it must state that evidence could not be gathered within recovery bounds so the finalizer scores the criterion unmet/indeterminate, not met. Aggregate char bound and finalizer input bound stay as-is. CompletionRecoveryError raised only when zero criteria produced evidence, carrying counts {criteria_total, criteria_exhausted}.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A single criterion's LLMBudgetExhaustedError no longer aborts recovery: with N criteria and one evidence run exhausting, the finalizer still runs and receives N evidence entries, the exhausted one carrying an explicit could-not-gather-within-bounds placeholder (unit test, held-out oracle style).\n- [x] A RunawayToolLoopError raised by an evidence run is handled the same way (unit test).\n- [x] A token-exhaustion UnretryableOutputError from an evidence run is converted to the exhausted placeholder, mirroring the primary path; a NON-token UnretryableOutputError still propagates (unit test).\n- [x] The placeholder is content-free (no exception prose interpolated beyond the failure class name and numeric usage counters) and can never read as affirmative evidence (unit test asserts wording).\n- [x] If EVERY criterion's evidence run fails, recovery raises CompletionRecoveryError with diagnostic {criteria_total, criteria_exhausted} (unit test).\n- [x] Successful-evidence behaviour is byte-identical: runs where no evidence agent fails produce the same finalizer input as before (unit test).\n- [x] Live Bedrock proof before ship: a real gate-style recovery over multiple criteria where at least one evidence run exhausts completes with a verdict instead of failing whole (session experiment, not in unit suite).\n- [x] make lint and mypy clean; full CI marker suite matches the pre-existing baseline.\n\n## Testing\nHeld-out unit oracle in tests/unit/workflow/ (written before the fix, RED first): `python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/ -q`. Mutation checks on the fix. Live Bedrock experiment (session artifact, not in unit suite) proving a multi-criterion recovery with one exhausted evidence run still reaches a verdict. `make lint` + `make typecheck` clean; full marker suite matches pre-existing baseline.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py","reason":"per-criterion evidence loop: catch budget/runaway exhaustion, placeholder entry, all-failed aggregate error"},{"path":"tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_recovery_evidence_ed6d.py","reason":"new held-out oracle for partial-evidence recovery"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","10ae-aa24-3fdc-4f0b"],["relates_to","2948-48e5-666f-4677"],["relates_to","f80f-7776-02aa-4091"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"10ae-aa24-3fdc-4f0b","parent_status_uuid":"d2deeb4d-4ee0-4682-87ce-4ec6b71ccbf2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"ed6d-5448-4ff6-4b8a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bounded recovery dies whole when one criterion's evidence run exhausts its budget","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7fc03137-5fb6-42c7-9ee6-dff2c3d67e80","b30079f7-9321-4a5e-8292-bdfa3f62065d","05d1b0d4-aac1-4a08-bfb9-722163396e0e","59603ea2-53f4-4803-a178-3ca9eda13dc4","db0a922e-e538-4870-b388-93a1f555ef10","f8b85845-db19-4264-9a54-6e2ccd6483af","3c4bfe13-57ca-4839-9236-7ab5c559b748","4f7a22dc-cfc4-4be4-9963-39047dfa6a45","e3adb322-514c-4f1a-af40-1baea64b61b5","9127493e-ae8b-4d6d-a9a1-1ecc5324a6f3","da3896c1-9570-47ec-ba76-d0b08ef89aaf","d2deeb4d-4ee0-4682-87ce-4ec6b71ccbf2","ed32c287-8995-4fd7-bc05-4d721b70e5ea","8db63530-75eb-427a-a9d3-db86b0cdb148","da9d42cc-baf3-4eba-8e75-93fb6f193bdc","a3681f44-9877-452e-9db8-339f5f671ecd"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786056142897165002,"uuid":"aad264b9-470e-4b20-84c3-a7bbfb5844f8"}